# Gunvalkyrie (49470017; the Nova's iso is 5345000B-Gunvalkyrie.xiso.iso),
# Nova. Built from the generic survey 1790921696-titleroutes-1084287
# (lane.titleroutes session 63, reviewed session 64; re-read by
# lane.titleroutes2 session 1, 2026-10-02). Read from its route-frames, not
# guessed:
#   booted (005249): the ADX logo, start of the intro movie.
#   cycle 1 (005254 START / 005300 A): a "VALLEY 1 now loading" card (the
#     attract demo loading).
#   cycle 2 (005307 START / 005313 A): "now loading", then the intro art.
#   cycle 3 (005318 START / 005324 A): "Please press START to begin", then
#     NEW GAME / CONTINUE / OPTIONS.
#   cycle 4 (005330 / 005335): black (New Game's opening movie).
#   cycle 5 (005342 START / 005348 A): the briefing menu (NEXT STAGE, POWER
#     UP, FOE'S REPORT, SAVE, LOAD, OPTIONS, EXIT), then the Valley 1 map.
#   cycle 6 (005354 START / 005359 A): GO / MISSION OUTLINE / ENEMY /
#     CAUTION / BACK, then character select (Kelly).
#   cycle 7 (005405 START / 005411 A): "Send to insertion point? YES", then
#     "VALLEY 1 now loading".
#   cycle 8 (005418 START / 005423 A): the STAGE 1 Valley 1 card, then live
#     play (the HUD, Kelly warping in).
#   cycles 9-14: START opens the pause panel (Continue highlighted) and A
#     picks Continue, so a START/A pair in play is pause + resume.
#   play (005605): the tip "While jumping, pull the Left Trigger again to
#     perform a Rocket Boost" -- LT is jump/boost.
# So: 10 START/A cycles (8 reached play; the last 2 are a guard against a
# slower boot, and pause + resume if play came on time), mark, then a play
# loop with no START: forward on the left stick, RT fire, LT jumps, RX
# turns so a wall does not hold it. One A per cycle (the survey pressed A
# in play with no visible effect) also takes a Continue/Retry panel if one
# comes up.
# Replay 1 (1790939914-titleroutes2-1445425, ref 282a5af148): no ROUTE FAIL;
# the title came one cycle sooner (play on cycle 7's START, 042146), the
# guard pairs were pause + Continue as planned, and the mark (042221) is
# live play with the HUD. But 9 of the 13 later frames are the advisor's
# tutorial boxes ("Use the Left Thumbstick to move...", "Pull the Right
# Trigger...", "...Dash in any direction while in the air"): the scene
# dims, the game waits, and a yellow down-arrow asks for A. One A per
# ~25 s cycle left each page up for most of a cycle. So the loop now
# presses A every ~2-3 s; the moves between are unchanged (the same run
# showed them working: walking, firing at 042347, static_frac 0.01).
# Replay 2 (1790940485-titleroutes2-1611958, ref 685c52e514): no ROUTE
# FAIL; the boxes now clear (2 of 14 post-mark frames show one); play the
# whole window, 100% at 30+, no hang. But from 044546 to 044755 Kelly faces
# one cliff face: the loop's turns nearly cancel (0.7 s right, 0.4 s left),
# so a wall ahead holds her for minutes. So the right-stick turn is now
# 1.2 s one way per cycle (the view sweeps round in a few cycles), and the
# jump is the tip's double pull of LT (jump, then Rocket Boost) to clear
# low rock.
# Replay 3 (1790941860-titleroutes2-2053231, ref 82ca509265): no ROUTE
# FAIL, play the whole window, 100% at 30+, no hang, static_frac 0.009 --
# but most frames are still Kelly against a canyon wall (051506-051555,
# 051733-051838). A 1.2 s turn per cycle only randomises her heading. The
# mark frame shows the spawn heading looking DOWN the canyon at the arch,
# and replay 1, which turned least, was the one that reached the arch
# (042255). So v4 never turned: forward the whole cycle, alternate 1.5 s
# strafes, the double-LT boost.
# Replay 4 (1790944628-titleroutes2-2686999, ref bd03a589f7): worse. She
# meets a dark rock face within 14 s of the mark and from 060508 to the end
# is pressed against one wall. Same numbers as every replay (59.94 median,
# 100% at 30+, 96% at 60, no hang, static 0.010): the canyon walls do not
# move the frame rate, they only make the window a poor picture of play.
# FINAL: the loop below is replay 2's (685c52e514) again, unchanged -- the
# one that travelled most (2.5 min at one cliff, then down the canyon) --
# so replay 2 is its confirmation run. Moving Kelly through Valley 1 for a
# whole window needs a screen-aware loop (drive.py), not a fifth blind one.
wait 20
shot boot20
wait 20
shot boot40
wait 20
shot booted
repeat 10 {
    press START
    wait 5
    shot menu-start
    press A
    wait 5
    shot menu-a
}
wait 2
shot pre-mark
mark gameplay               # CHECK: Valley 1, the HUD, no pause panel over it
repeat forever {
    press A
    axis LY min
    axis RT max
    wait 2
    axis RT min
    press A
    axis LT max
    wait 0.3
    axis LT min
    wait 1.5
    press A
    axis RX max
    wait 0.7
    axis RX mid
    axis RT max
    wait 2
    axis RT min
    press A
    axis LY mid
    axis LX max
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
    press A
    axis LY min
    wait 2
    axis RX min
    wait 0.4
    axis RX mid
    press A
    wait 1
    shot play
}
